t?\nPeebee: Take a wild guess. Why are people so hung up on sex? It's a natural expression of attraction.\nPeebee: We were doing exciting, daring, irreverent things. It stirs stuff up. Like shaking up a bottle of champagne, you know?\nPeebee: You should know, better than anyone...\nPeebee: I'm not the type to \"save myself\".", "reference": "2017, BioWare, Mass Effect: Andromeda (Science Fiction), Redwood City: Electronic Arts, →OCLC, PC, scene: Tempest:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(informal) To avoid saying something.", "tags": ["informal"], "examples": ["Save your excuses and lies."], "quotes": [{"text": "School days went by. I ran across Sly a couple a times, but I wasn't in no mood to talk. He could save all that philosophical bullshit he liked to holla. Didn't nobody need to tell me what was up.", "reference": "2006, Noire [pseudonym], Thug-A-Licious: An Urban Erotic Tale, New York, N.Y.: One World, Ballantine Books, →ISBN, page 206:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}]}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/seɪv/", "tags": ["General American", "Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/sæɪv/", "tags": ["General Australian", "New Zealand"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/sev/", "tags": ["Scotland"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/seːv/", "tags": ["Wales"]}], "forms": [{"word": "saves", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "An instance of preventing (further) harm or difficulty.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "As 1942 began, work was now continuing apace on getting the ships back afloat and into dock. The first good news in this regard was West Virginia. Thanks to a combination of Tennessees unintentional save' and the crew's own efforts, she'd settled upright, and so divers estimated that, if the various holes could be patched and pumping done in a sensible order from the top down, she should just rise back up to the surface on an even keel, which, in turn, meant that a lot of the initial work on removing her main battery could now be stopped.", "reference": "2020 November 18, Drachinifel, 0:34 from the start, in The Salvage of Pearl Harbor Pt 2 - Up She Rises!, archived from the original on 22 Oct 2022:"}, {"text": "It is no coincidence that two of the four 'saves' on our tour connect with the early days of the Stockton & Darlington Railway (S&DR), where restoration has also been helped by recent research that explains further why these saves are so significant.", "reference": "2025 February 5, Dr Joseph Brennan, “Railway heritage saved in 2024”, in RAIL, number 1028, page 53:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": [{"definition": "In various sports, a block that prevents an opponent from scoring.", "tags": [], "examples": ["The goaltender made a great save."], "quotes": [{"text": "Wolves defender Ronald Zubar was slightly closer with his shot on the turn as he forced Pepe Reina, on his 200th Premier League appearance, into a low save.", "reference": "2010 December 29, Sam Sheringham, “Liverpool 0 - 1 Wolverhampton”, in BBC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "спасяване"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "aturada"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "redning"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "tõrje"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "torjunta"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "arrêt"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "απόκρουση"}, {"language": {"code": "ga", "name": "Irish"}, "word": "sábháil"}, {"language": {"code": "it", "name": "Italian"}, "word": "parata"}, {"language": {"code": "no", "name": "Norwegian"}, "word": "redning"}, {"langu